# --- Secrets: the compliance-relevant section -------------------------------
# A committed secret is a reportable event, not a cleanup task. Once it is in
# git history it must be treated as disclosed and rotated, even after removal.
# This list is defense-in-depth only; the real control is never writing a
# secret to disk inside a repo in the first place.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.publishsettings
azureauth.json
auth0-config.json
*.secrets.json
secrets/

# --- Personal, per-machine Claude Code config -------------------------------
# Shared config (.claude/settings.json, .mcp.json, skills, rules) IS committed:
# it is part of how the project is reproduced. Only per-person state is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/logs/

# --- Real patient data ------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here should ever exist. The pattern is a tripwire: if git ever has
# cause to ignore one of these, something has already gone wrong.
*.phi.*
*-real-data.*
patient-export*

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.venv/
__pycache__/
